# LongCat 2.5 Preview — findings by Big Pickle

- Source: Meituan (`longcat-2.5-preview`)
- Date: 2026-10-02 (UTC)
- Overview and scoring methodology: `../../model-comparison.md`
- Cross-model signed log: `../../model-findings.md`

## Model card

- **Name:** LongCat 2.5 Preview
- **Short description:** Meituan's 1.6T-parameter mixture-of-experts model for long-horizon
  agent work, released 2026-09-25 as a preview: 1M-token context, native image input added on
  top of the LongCat-2.0 base, and no vendor benchmark table at launch. Meituan shipped **no
  model card, no technical report and no benchmark numbers** for it; everything below comes
  from vendor API documentation plus one independent coding-leaderboard measurement.
- **Provider / access:** Meituan LongCat API platform (OpenAI-compatible Chat Completions and
  Anthropic-compatible Messages endpoints, both documented) and OpenCode Zen as
  `opencode/longcat-2.5-preview-free`. Chat API exposes a switchable `thinking` setting;
  reasoning traces arrive interleaved as `reasoning_content`.
- **Release / knowledge:** 2026-09-25 (vendor changelog entry "LongCat-2.5-Preview Now
  Available"). Knowledge cutoff not published by Meituan.
- **IDs:** `meituan/longcat-2.5-preview` (Vercel AI Gateway), `LongCat-2.5-Preview` (vendor),
  `opencode/longcat-2.5-preview-free` (OpenCode Zen — free tier of the same weights).
- **Context window:** 1,048,576 tokens (1M) total, 131,072 max output — vendor API quick-start
  docs plus Vercel AI Gateway and models.dev metadata, all agreeing. Longest published value is
  the spec; **no retrieval benchmark at that length is reported**.
- **Modalities:** text + image in (vendor changelog: image understanding for cross-modal QA,
  summarisation, visual reasoning); text out; reasoning yes (toggle); tool calling yes. One
  secondary write-up adds "video / screen-recording" input, but no vendor doc or model listing
  confirms it, so it is not counted.
- **Pricing (as of 2026-10-02):** free through OpenCode Zen (`longcat-2.5-preview-free`) — "free
  for a limited time", unlimited, zero data retention, not used for training. Direct Meituan
  pay-as-you-go: **$0.30 / $1.20 per 1M in/out**, cached input $0.006 / 1M, flagged by the vendor
  page as a limited-time discounted rate with no published end date. Meituan's X account said
  "two weeks" on 2026-09-26, which points at roughly 2026-10-10 — treat the free window as
  expiring without notice.
- **Architecture:** proprietary MoE, ~1.6T total / ~48B active per token (~3% active). Weights
  **not** released — the previous LongCat-2.0 was MIT-licensed on Hugging Face, this preview is
  API-only.

### Raw benchmarks found

Agent / tool use:

- Terminal-Bench 2.1: **no verified public score found** (vendor published none; the 70.8 figure
  in circulation belongs to LongCat-2.0, a different model — provisional family proxy only)
- Tau3-Banking / Tau2-Bench: **no verified public score found**
- GDPval-AA: **no verified public score found**
- Claw-Eval / ClawProBench: **no verified public score found**
- Toolathon / MCP-Atlas / SWE Atlas Codebase QnA: **no verified public score found**
- AI Coding Daily LLM Coding Leaderboard (agentic harness run, OpenCode): **46.65 / 80 points,
  rank 36**, measured 2026-10-02 — the only independent measured score found for this exact ID.
  Per-project breakdown: Laravel Code Quality 16.98/20, React-TS Code Quality 16.67/20, Bug
  Finding Test 2.4/20, CSV Import (PHP) 3/20, Offline Sync (PHP) 2.7/20, Bank Feed
  (Dart/Flutter) 4/20, Shipping Quotes (Go) 0.9/20. Avg time per prompt 16:50; cost N/A (free
  tier). For calibration on the same board and date: GPT-6.1-Sol (High) 68.1, Opus 5.5 (High)
  67.41, Qwen 3.8 27B 47.76, GLM-5.3-Flash 47.51, Gemini-3.8-Flash 47.09, GPT-6-Luna (Medium)
  43.74, Gemini-3.1-Pro 42.36.
  (An earlier snapshot of the same board showed 44.25 at rank 34 on 2026-09-28 — same harness,
  same per-project numbers, slightly different total; the 2026-10-02 figure is the current one.)

Reasoning / knowledge:

- GPQA Diamond: **no verified public score found**
- HLE: **no verified public score found**
- LCR / MLCR: **no verified public score found**
- CritPt: **no verified public score found**
- Artificial Analysis Intelligence Index / BenchLM overall: **no verified public score found**
  (the model does not appear on Artificial Analysis; the LongCat-2.0 comparison pages there are a
  different model)
- Omniscience Accuracy / Hallucination Rate: **no verified public score found**
- Provisional family proxy (LongCat-2.0, 2026-06-30, MIT weights — same 1.6T/48B backbone but
  text-only and not this model): Artificial Analysis Intelligence Index 34, Terminal-Bench 2.1
  70.8, SWE-bench Multilingual 77.3, SWE-bench Pro 59.5. Do not read these as 2.5 Preview
  results.

Coding:

- SWE-bench Verified / SWE-Pro: **no verified public score found** for this ID (59.5 SWE-bench
  Pro is the 2.0 figure)
- LiveCodeBench: **no verified public score found**
- SciCode / AA-SciCode: **no verified public score found**
- Vibe Code Bench: **no verified public score found**
- AI Coding Daily per-project coding scores (OpenCode harness, 2026-10-02): Laravel 16.98/20 and
  React-TS 16.67/20 — strong front-end scaffolding; Shipping Quotes (Go) 0.9/20, Offline Sync
  (PHP) 2.7/20, Bug Finding 2.4/20 — near-failure on multi-step and multi-language logic work.

Long context:

- **no long-context retrieval reported.** 1M tokens is a documented spec, with no MRCR, RULER,
  GraphWalks or recall number at any length from Meituan or from any third party.

### Normalized scores (1–100)

- **Tool use: 58/100.** Tool calling is declared and the vendor lists deep compatibility with
  Claude Code, OpenCode, Kilo Code, OpenClaw and Hermes, and the one independent measurement we
  have (a real tool-driven agent harness) shows solid completion on structured UI work. Capped
  by the complete absence of Terminal-Bench / Tau3 / GDPval / Claw-Eval numbers for this ID and
  by weak scores on the tasks that need planning plus verification (bug finding 2.4/20), with a
  16:50 average per prompt.
- **Reasoning: not scored (was 52/100 — score withdrawn 2026-10-05).** The 52 was anchored on
  the LongCat-2.0 sibling's Artificial Analysis Intelligence Index of 34. That is a **different
  model** — text-only, MIT-weights, superseded — and `RULES.md` forbids transferring one model's
  numbers to another. With the anchor removed, **zero** reasoning measurements exist for this ID:
  no GPQA, no HLE, no LCR, no CritPt, no Index, no Omniscience. Thinking mode is *declared* but
  never measured. Any number here would be a placeholder in disguise, which drags the folder mean
  for every reader, so the dimension is left explicitly unscored rather than filled. This is the
  single reason the whole file stays excluded: Tool use and Coding rest on one community
  leaderboard run, Context and Multimodal rest on verified specs, Cost rests on a verified $0
  tier — Reasoning has no measurable subject at all.
- **Context window: 96/100.** 1,048,576 tokens (1M) is verified by vendor docs, Vercel and
  models.dev, with a 131,072 max output. Tier mapping puts ≥1M at 95–100; 100 would require
  ≥98% retrieval measured at 512K+, and nothing has been measured, so it sits just below the top
  of the band.
- **Multimodal: 65/100.** Native image input is claimed in the vendor changelog and flagged by
  the models.dev attachment flag, which maps to the +image-in band at 60–70. No audio input and
  no non-text output; no independent vision benchmark to lift it further. The "video input"
  claim in one secondary write-up is unconfirmed and not counted.
- **Coding: 60/100.** The only independent measurement puts it mid-pack at 46.65/80 (rank 36),
  above Gemini-3.1-Pro and Composer 2.5, below GPT-6-Luna (Medium) — with a sharp internal split:
  excellent on Laravel and React-TS UI generation, close to zero on Go quoting, PHP offline sync
  and bug finding. Provisional family scores (SWE-Pro 59.5, TB2.1 70.8) are not transferable to
  this ID and do not lift the score.
- **Cost efficiency: 100/100.** Free through OpenCode Zen right now, unlimited and zero
  retention. Flagged as time-limited: the paid fallback is $0.30 / $1.20 per 1M, which is
  cheap-but-paid territory, and neither the Zen window nor the vendor discount carries a
  published end date.
- **Overall Score: not scored (was 66.2/100 — score withdrawn 2026-10-05).** The 66.2 was the
  half-up mean of 58 / 52 / 96 / 65 / 60 and is **void**, because one of its five inputs (the
  LongCat-2.0-derived Reasoning 52) has been withdrawn. A mean cannot survive the removal of a
  component without silently becoming a different number, so it is retired rather than
  recomputed. The remaining four dims average 69.75, but that figure is **not** an Overall: with
  Reasoning missing, the five-dim mean the methodology mandates cannot be formed at all. This is
  the mechanical reason the file stays `.md.excluded`. (Cost is excluded from Overall regardless.)
  For what the evidence does support, un-averaged: Context 96 and Cost 100 are on verified specs
  and a verified $0 tier; Tool use 58 and Coding 60 rest on a single community leaderboard run.
  Best fit if you use it anyway: a free, 1M-context, image-capable executor for UI scaffolding
  and bulk file work while the free window lasts — not as the planner of record.

